,"text":"]"}],"title":"minimumVertexCover(bipartition:)","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"König’s minimum vertex cover of a bipartite graph (NetworkX "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"to_vertex_cover"},{"type":"text","text":", the same"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"cover): from a maximum matching (Hopcroft–Karp on the sides), Z is the set of vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"reached from the free left vertices by alternating paths, an edge not in the matching from"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"left to right, then the matched edge back; the cover is (left ∖ Z) ∪ (right ∩ Z), in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" order. It is the one minimum cover with the most left vertices, so it does not"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"depend on the matching. O(m √n)."}],"url":"\/documentation\/covering\/graphprotocols\/graph\/minimumvertexcover(bipartition:)"},"doc://Covering/documentation/Covering/GraphProtocols/Graph/maximumIndependentSet()":{"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/covering\/graphprotocols\/graph\/maximumindependentset()","role":"symbol","title":"maximumIndependentSet()","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A maximum independent set (exact): of all the largest ones, the lexicographically least by"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertex index, in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" order; [] for the empty graph. Of two sets of one size, the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"lesser holds the least vertex of their symmetric difference ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"maximumClique()"},{"type":"text","text":"’s rule, so"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"on a loop-free graph this is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"maximumClique()"},{"type":"text","text":" of the complement). A vertex with a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"