xt"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Covering\/documentation\/Covering\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/independenceNumber()","title":"independenceNumber()","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/covering\/graphprotocols\/graph\/independencenumber()","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"independenceNumber","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","text":"Int","kind":"typeIdentifier"}]},"doc://Covering/documentation/Covering/GraphProtocols/Graph/approximateMinimumVertexCover(weight:)":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A vertex cover of at most twice the least weight (Bar-Yehuda and Even’s local ratio; NetworkX"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"min_weighted_vertex_cover"},{"type":"text","text":", the same cover when positions are in its edge order): each edge"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"in position order with neither end in the cover puts in the end with the lesser remaining"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"weight (the end with the lesser vertex index on ties) and subtracts that weight from the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"other end’s. A self-loop puts its vertex in. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"weight"},{"type":"text","text":" is called once per vertex, in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" order. O(n + m)."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Covering\/documentation\/Covering\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/approximateMinimumVertexCover(weight:)","title":"approximateMinimumVertexCover(weight:)","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/covering\/graphprotocols\/graph\/approximateminimumvertexcover(weight:)","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"approximateMinimumVertexCover","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"W","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":"